<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.5.5: Writing Equations to Represent Exponential Decay</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01329</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.5.5: Writing Equations to Represent Exponential Decay</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6097bbe2-beb1-4be9-ab69-1d295ad94be3</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <para>Acetaminophen is a common pain reliever and fever reducer. Here is a graph showing the amount of acetaminophen, in milligrams, in an adult’s body at different times after they take a normal dose.</para>
      <para>
          <media alt="Graph of an exponential function, origin O. time (hours) and acetaminophen (mg).">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_07_12_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Answer the following questions.</para>
        <para>What is the vertical intercept?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>1,000</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What does it mean in this situation?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>There are 1,000 mg of acetaminophen in the person’s body after taking the medicine (this is the dose size).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What fraction of the medicine remained after one hour?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(\frac34\) of the medicine remained after 1 hour since \(\frac{750}{1000}=\frac{3}{4}\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>Write an equation that represents the amount of medicine, \(a\), after \(t\) hours.</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
  </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>\(a=1,000(\frac{3}{4})^t\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
